0006: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0007:     """
0008:     Fill the region enclosed by a wall sprite and radiate color outward through its opening.
0009: 
0010:     Input structure:
0011:     - bg = most common color. Wall = most frequent non-bg color, forming a partial enclosure (e.g. U-shape).
0012:     - A fill-color pixel sits inside the enclosed area. Other non-bg pixels may act as obstacles.
0013:     Rule:
0014:     - Flood-fill the enclosed area with the fill color, radiating outward through the wall's open end.
0015:     - Obstacles cast "shadows" along the radiate direction, blocking fill behind them.
0016: 
0017:     Key insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.
